{
  "duration": 79.319,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.299,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.839,
      "end": 2.019,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.599,
      "end": 4.299,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.819,
      "end": 5.639,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.079,
      "end": 8.439,
      "text": "a point is thirty meters away from a building."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.939,
      "end": 9.96,
      "text": "From that same point,"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.34,
      "end": 13.02,
      "text": "the angle of elevation to the top of the building is"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.46,
      "end": 14.439,
      "text": "thirty degrees,"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.88,
      "end": 18.34,
      "text": "and the angle of elevation to the top of the flagstaff is sixty degrees."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.659,
      "end": 21.279,
      "text": "We need to find only the height of the flagstaff."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.619,
      "end": 22.979,
      "text": "Let the height of the building be"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.279,
      "end": 23.84,
      "text": "h meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.199,
      "end": 25.759,
      "text": "Let the height of the flagstaff be"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.099,
      "end": 26.639,
      "text": "x meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.059,
      "end": 30.479,
      "text": "So the total height up to the top of the flagstaff will be h plus"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.819,
      "end": 30.879,
      "text": "x."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.679,
      "end": 33.139,
      "text": "Using the tangent formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.719,
      "end": 36.119,
      "text": "ten theta is equal to opposite by adjacent."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.559,
      "end": 37.759,
      "text": "First, for the building,"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.18,
      "end": 40.719,
      "text": "ten thirty degrees is equal to h by thirty."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.219,
      "end": 43.5,
      "text": "So h is equal to thirty by root three."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.939,
      "end": 46.399,
      "text": "That means h is equal to ten root three meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.779,
      "end": 48.319,
      "text": "Now, for the top of the flagstaff,"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.84,
      "end": 52.279,
      "text": "ten sixty degrees is equal to h plus x by thirty."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.799,
      "end": 55.619,
      "text": "So h plus x is equal to thirty root three."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.279,
      "end": 59.579,
      "text": "This is the total height, building plus flagstaff."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.979,
      "end": 61.619,
      "text": "Now we need only the flagstaff height."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.0,
      "end": 62.239,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.559,
      "end": 69.399,
      "text": "x is equal to total height minus building height. X is equal to thirty root three minus ten root three."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.919,
      "end": 73.099,
      "text": "So x is equal to twenty root three meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.919,
      "end": 77.139,
      "text": "So the final answer will be twenty root three meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.58,
      "end": 79.319,
      "text": "That means option C is correct."
    }
